{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described","id":1392934,"title":"Where are Fatigue Penalties Described?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-30T16:41:05-07:00","id":1392934,"title":"Where are Fatigue Penalties Described?","content":"Just going through some of the Dragon-Blooded Charms and ran across Untiring Earth Mediation that states that as long as they are touching the Earth (rock, sand, etc.) that they can ignore all fatigue penalties... but i can't find &quot;fatigue&quot; penalties described anywhere in the Core book (3E). I do see a brief description of penalties, but not specifically &quot;fatigue&quot;. Any help (page reference ideally) would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T16:55:21-07:00","id":1392941,"title":"","content":"I believe right now &quot;fatigue&quot; penalties are mostly just like &quot;environmental&quot; penalties, or &quot;visual&quot; penalties. Apart from a scant few spells like Travel Without Distance nothing specifically calls it out, but Storytellers should start applying fatigue penalties to rolls if the characters have been running exhaustively or staying awake for long periods of time, just like they should introduce visual penalties to bow shots through fog and environmental penalties to evasion on slick rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:05:32-07:00","id":1392947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>Deprivation</b></u> (p. 232)<br /> Exalts and mortals both share the basic necessities of<br /> life\u2014air, water, and food. A character will suffocate or<br /> drown after (Stamina) minutes without air, die of dehydration<br /> after (Stamina) days without water, and perish<br /> from starvation after (Stamina) weeks without food.<br /> Characters suffer a -3 penalty to all actions after (Stamina)<br /> days without food, as well as in their final hours without<br /> water. </div> </div> </div>I guess? <br /> <br /> There's also a ruling that you can operate without sleep for Resistance + Stamina days but god help me if I can find it. Sometimes the layout of the book is to helter-skelter for me. <br /> <br /> P.480 <b>Travel Without Distance </b>imposes fatigue penalties. Boundless Endurance P 159 helps resist fatigue penalties, but you are right, the book does not say anything about imposing them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:08:19-07:00","id":1392949,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember, I think, that 3e really assumes that the ST will be fairly free with applying penalties when they're applicable. Not much in the book explicitly imposes fatigue penalties, sure, but they clearly exist, since various things negate them. So, they should be applied. If the characters have just run a marathon to get to the battlefield before all is lost, most of them should be panting and gasping, with only the DBs with Untiring Earth Meditation or others with similar charms being able to still act unhindered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:24:04-07:00","id":1392950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described?p=1392947#post1392947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a ruling that you can operate without sleep for Resistance + Stamina days but god help me if I can find it. Sometimes the layout of the book is to helter-skelter for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 232 for deprivation. Stamina minutes without air, Stamina days without water, Stamina weeks without food. Air gets shortened to 2xStamina rounds if your overly exerting yourself such as in combat. You suffer a -3 penalty to all actions after Stamina days without food, as well as the final hours without water. I would also modify the water and food stuff contextually too. You can't survive that long while marching in full armor through a dune sea in summer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:20:12-07:00","id":1392975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described?p=1392949#post1392949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember, I think, that 3e really assumes that the ST will be fairly free with applying penalties when they're applicable. Not much in the book explicitly imposes fatigue penalties, sure, but they clearly exist, since various things negate them. So, they should be applied. If the characters have just run a marathon to get to the battlefield before all is lost, most of them should be panting and gasping, with only the DBs with Untiring Earth Meditation or others with similar charms being able to still act unhindered.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have been nice to make this more clear. Just the existence of Fatigue-Negating abilities isn't enough of a guide about how fatigue works. There's a whole page for Feats of Strength, a list of Environmental penalties, a guide for Sailing hazards, a list of eating, drinking, and breathing rules, so it seems a little bit like an oversight that Fatigue is mentioned but not explained. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described?p=1392950#post1392950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 232 for deprivation. Stamina minutes without air, Stamina days without water, Stamina weeks without food. Air gets shortened to 2xStamina rounds if your overly exerting yourself such as in combat. You suffer a -3 penalty to all actions after Stamina days without food, as well as the final hours without water. I would also modify the water and food stuff contextually too. You can't survive that long while marching in full armor through a dune sea in summer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really useful information, which why I quoted that exact passage in my post too. My specific remark was about <b>sleep deprivation</b> however. <br /> <br /> I went through all 87 matches to the word Sleep in the corebook pdf and I can't find anything that talks about sleep deprivation. Lots of stuff reset on a good night's sleep, some spells and charms affect sleepers, but i didn't see one single rule that says &quot;Here is how hard sleep resistance is&quot;. The blurb about Stamina mentions its useful to stay awake but not how to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:37:26-07:00","id":1392978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described?p=1392975#post1392975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really useful information, which why I quoted that exact passage in my post too. My specific remark was about <b>sleep deprivation</b> however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, duh, I see a quote at the top of somebody's post and assume they're just quoting the person they're responding to...so..yeah..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T20:18:17-07:00","id":1392990,"title":"","content":"haha, it's all good man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T07:01:46-07:00","id":1393077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1392934-where-are-fatigue-penalties-described?p=1392950#post1392950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 232 for deprivation. Stamina minutes without air, Stamina days without water, Stamina weeks without food. Air gets shortened to 2xStamina rounds if your overly exerting yourself such as in combat. You suffer a -3 penalty to all actions after Stamina days without food, as well as the final hours without water. I would also modify the water and food stuff contextually too. You can't survive that long while marching in full armor through a dune sea in summer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unfortunately, the Dragon-Blooded have charms that specifically deal with these Deprivation effects (Uneating Earth Meditation for starvation/dehydration, Unsleeping Earth meditation for lack of sleep and Unbreathing Earth Meditation for suffocation). It would seem that Unfatiguing Earth Meditation is intended to deal with exhaustion from intense physical activity, like running full out or lifting huge weights for extended periods of time... the problem is that there is no real definition for what counts as fatigue. How long can one hold a feat of strength up? How long can the run at maximum speed? When does combat become exhausting when wearing heavy armor? With no real guideline to apply fatigue penalties, there really is no way to judge when this charm will be needed, more or less rendering it (and similar charms) useless outside of magics that specifically impose such penalties.<br /> <br /> Kind of frustrating, but not much that can be done except trying to deal with what seems appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T17:27:07-07:00","id":1393262,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m hoping that Crucible of Legends will have info on when to assign penalties and all that good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}